=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: laptop0
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The IPv4 default route / gateway address on laptop0.

**Mechanism:** laptop0 is configured with a default gateway of `172.16.20.99`, but no device in the topology owns that IP address on the VLAN 20 segment. When laptop0 attempts to send any packet outside its directly-connected subnet (`172.16.20.0/24`), the kernel must ARP-resolve `172.16.20.99` to obtain a next-hop MAC. Because `172.16.20.99` is a phantom address, ARP probes go unanswered, the neighbor entry enters `FAILED` state, and the kernel discards every outbound packet that requires forwarding. Same-VLAN peers (laptop2, laptop3) remain reachable because the `172.16.20.0/24` connected route bypasses the default gateway entirely; no ARP for the gateway is needed within the subnet.

**Localization:** The fault is entirely contained within laptop0 (`172.16.20.10`). Its eth0 interface is UP and correctly addressed (`172.16.20.10/24`). The VLAN 20 gateway on router0 is the sub-interface `eth0.20` at `172.16.20.1/24`, which is present and healthy. VLAN 10 hosts (pc4/pc5) and all other devices are unaffected.

**Root cause:** laptop0 has an incorrect default gateway (`172.16.20.99`) instead of the correct VLAN 20 router address (`172.16.20.1`).

**Fix:** Replace the default route on laptop0: remove `default via 172.16.20.99 dev eth0` and add `default via 172.16.20.1 dev eth0`. This restores next-hop reachability to router0's VLAN 20 sub-interface and re-establishes full cross-VLAN routing.
=== END ===